  "label": "Colonialism and Race",
  "description": "The deep connection between colonialism and racial hierarchies, in which colonizers often justified their domination by constructing racialized narratives that portrayed colonized peoples as inferior, primitive, or uncivilized. This racialized discourse was used to legitimize exploitation and violence, and its effects continue to shape global racial dynamics and power structures.",
